course: dictionary
lesson: 9122
title: Smoky: full of smoke, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Smoky has three main meanings. It can mean full of smoke, as in «a smoky room». It can mean smelling or tasting of smoke, as in «smoky bacon». It can also describe a grey colour like smoke, as in «smoky grey».
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. In «Hot smoke rises, so the cleanest air in a smoky room is near the floor», the word smoke tells you that smoky means full of smoke. Then try your meaning in the sentence: a room full of smoke makes sense here.
explain: Smoky is an adjective, so it can change form: smokier means more smoky, and smokiest means the most smoky. Ask yourself what the word describes, a room, a taste or a colour, and that tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Smoky means full of smoke, smelling of smoke, or grey like smoke.
fact: Smokier means more smoky, and smokiest means the most smoky.
fact: In a smoky room, the cleanest air is near the floor, because hot smoke rises.
fact: Smoke alarms warn us early, so we can get out and call the fire service.
fact: In smoky 1800s England, soot blackened tree trunks, so dark moths hid better.
exercise: What does «a smoky room» mean? | Full of water | Painted bright pink | *Full of smoke | Very cold and empty
exercise: What does «smoky bacon» taste of? | Lemon juice and salt | *Smoke, from a barbecue or smoked food | Sugar and mint | Ice cream and syrup
exercise: «In smoky 1800s England, soot blackened tree trunks.» What did the soot do to the tree trunks? | *Made them dark | Made them pale | Painted them green | Washed them clean
test: What does «smoky» mean in «smoky grey»? | Smelling of smoke | Shiny and wet | *Grey, like smoke | Full of smoke
test: «Hot smoke rises, so the cleanest air in a smoky room is near the floor.» Where is the cleanest air? | In the middle of the room | At the ceiling | *Near the floor | Outside the window
exam: Why should you stay low if a room is smoky? | *Because the cleanest air is near the floor | Because it is quieter down there | Because smoke is heavy and sinks down | Because the floor is warm and cosy
